  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, in `src/store.js` and `src/api.js`. `npm test` passes: 175 tests, 0 failed, including the new ones.\n\n- **Store:** `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release` work as specified, using only the store's `clock`. `removeItem` now checks the quantity against available stock, so reserved stock can't be removed.\n- **API:** `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`. `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the statuses you listed.\n\nSome choices the spec left open:\n- **`confirm` return value:** `confirm(id)` returns `{ sku, qty }`, which the API uses to build its response.\n- **Expired reservations:** An expired reservation stays in memory rather than being removed, so confirming it again keeps returning `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` instead of `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`.\n- **Reservation ids:** Ids look like `res-1`, `res-2`.\n- **Unspecified inputs:** I added no validation for `ttlMs`, since the spec didn't ask for it. Any `POST /reservations` error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` returns 400.\n\nI added store tests for each rule, including expiry at exactly `creation + ttlMs`. I also added API tests for every status code.",
